      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:02:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding `allocateMultiView`: `BufferQueueProducer` allocates buffers internally via `GraphicBufferAllocator` / `IGraphicBufferProducer::requestBuffer`. In standard AOSP, `BufferQueue` does not have direct awareness of vendor-specific private bits like `1ULL \u003c\u003c 58`.\n\nHardcoding vendor/private Gralloc usage flags (`1ULL \u003c\u003c 58`) directly in an AOSP `libgui_test` will fail on generic targets, Cuttlefish, and non-Qualcomm allocators.\n\nTo address this properly:\n1. Multi-view allocation capabilities should be negotiated through standardized `AHardwareBuffer` / Gralloc usage flags or AIDL Allocator/Mapper interfaces.\n2. For platform GUI tests running across heterogeneous devices in CI, check whether multi-view allocation is supported by the underlying Gralloc / Mapper HAL, and call `GTEST_SKIP()` when unsupported rather than failing hard assertions.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "parentUuid": "5ce95e3a_3d316cbc",
      "revId": "0fe17401ae8dce453432c3700480eb590236951a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
