      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:02:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`dequeueBuffer` is called with `width \u003d 0, height \u003d 0, format \u003d 0` without setting default buffer dimensions or format on the producer/consumer queue beforehand.\n\nIt is recommended to either configure explicit test dimensions (e.g. `mProducer-\u003esetDefaultBufferSize(64, 64)`) and format (e.g. `HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBA_8888`), or pass explicit width, height, and format to `dequeueBuffer` to ensure deterministic allocation behavior across different Gralloc implementations.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "0fe17401ae8dce453432c3700480eb590236951a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
